From: cezanne port
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2codecs: DRM byte pitches in the VideoMeta of tiled DMA_DRM buffers

With DMA_DRM caps the pool's buffers carry the driver's layout in their
GstVideoMeta, and DMA_DRM consumers use the meta strides as the DRM plane
pitches (gtkgstsink passes them to EGL / Vulkan as the dmabuf pitch). For
tiled formats (MediaTek MM21 = NV12_16L32S with
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_MTK_16L_32S_TILE) GstVideoInfo stores the stride packed as
tile counts (GST_VIDEO_TILE_MAKE_STRIDE: y_tiles << 16 | x_tiles), so a
1280x720 frame was imported with a 0x170050 (1507408) byte pitch: Mesa's
panfrost detiled the first tile row and read zeros below it, and GTK
showed the video green. Convert the meta strides of tiled DMA_DRM buffers
to bytes; the GstVideoInfo (used by the element's own copies) keeps the
tile encoding.
---
 sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecpool.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

--- a/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecpool.c
+++ b/sys/v4l2codecs/gstv4l2codecpool.c
@@ -51,8 +51,10 @@
     GstBufferPoolAcquireParams * params)
 {
   GstV4l2CodecPool *self = GST_V4L2_CODEC_POOL (pool);
+  const GstVideoFormatInfo *finfo;
   GstBuffer *buf;
   GstVideoMeta *vmeta;
+  guint i;
 
   /* A GstVideoInfo must be set before buffer can be acquired */
   g_return_val_if_fail (self->vinfo_drm, GST_FLOW_ERROR);
@@ -93,6 +95,18 @@
   memcpy (vmeta->offset, self->vinfo_drm->vinfo.offset, sizeof (vmeta->offset));
   memcpy (vmeta->stride, self->vinfo_drm->vinfo.stride, sizeof (vmeta->stride));
 
+  /* DMA_DRM consumers (gtkgstsink, EGL / Vulkan dmabuf imports) take the
+   * meta strides as the DRM plane pitches, but GstVideoInfo keeps a tiled
+   * format's strides as packed tile counts (GST_VIDEO_TILE_MAKE_STRIDE):
+   * hand them the pitch in bytes, tile columns times a tile row. */
+  finfo = self->vinfo_drm->vinfo.finfo;
+  if (self->vinfo_drm->drm_fourcc /* != DRM_FORMAT_INVALID */  &&
+      GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_INFO_IS_TILED (finfo)) {
+    for (i = 0; i < vmeta->n_planes; i++)
+      vmeta->stride[i] = GST_VIDEO_TILE_X_TILES (vmeta->stride[i]) *
+          GST_VIDEO_FORMAT_INFO_TILE_STRIDE (finfo, i);
+  }
+
   *buffer = buf;
   return GST_FLOW_OK;
 }
